whitepaper: strip version/history language; cold-open present-tense

The paper was leaking review-process and self-history vocabulary
that breaks the cold-open contract: the reader has not read a
previous version, does not know about review rounds, and does not
need anxious gestures toward future work.

Stripped:
- "Mechanization Status v2.6" in the Reader's Map → "Formal
  Verification Status".
- "the v2.5-sealed Pareto-dominance artifact bundle" → the artifact
  bundle, accompanies this paper.
- "This is a real revision to the §youle mechanism design and is
  recorded honestly in the v2.6 cartel-resilience analysis" →
  "The single-instrument deposit policy is provably insufficient;
  the mechanism in §youle is correct only with this composite
  extension." (drops both the "real revision" and the "v2.6"
  framing.)
- "A formal Coq/Lean mechanization … is carried indefinitely
  behind the empirical artifact" → "is not in this paper; the
  empirical artifact stands on its own."
- "We identify this as future work requiring collaboration with
  economists" → "A full optimal-auction derivation in that
  tradition is outside the scope of this paper."
- "A review-process changelog, including the round-by-round
  dialogue between adversarial and white-hat fleets that produced
  the current status, is rendered at …" → dropped entirely from
  the Artifact Availability paragraph.
- "Earlier drafts dismissed the multi-node case as 'unnecessary
  for local development'" → present-tense framing of the federated
  trust model without the "earlier drafts" self-history.
- "Functional form: future work" → "The functional form is left
  open."
- "The Version~2 expansion threads six contributions through this
  skeleton" → "Six further contributions thread through this
  skeleton."
- "The advisory design … remains the correct resolution" → "is
  the correct resolution".
- "The central open problem---bond pricing---is no longer a single
  open problem" → "Bond pricing is not a single open problem."
- "Four mechanizations are carried indefinitely behind the
  empirical evidence" → "Four mechanizations are out of scope for
  this paper but explicitly named so a reader can audit what is
  and is not proved."
- "PROM-formal future work" → "PROM-formal version not in scope"
  (status-table cell).
- "the original draft promised in one paragraph … and now
  substantiates" → "This is the structural meaning of
  'decentralized verification' in this paper".
- "The original specification states the escrow invariant in TLA+
  but does not commit to an operational accounting. The April 2026
  implementation in lib/bonds.ts collapses…" → present-tense
  framing of the same content without dating the implementation
  or contrasting with an "original".

The remaining occurrences of "earlier" / "originally" / "previously"
in the text all refer to time-ordered events within the system
being described (a previously-assigned port, a capability originally
granted) rather than to paper revisions; those stay.

Page count: 37, build clean.


